For any learning algorithm $\pi$ that can use a total of $\Bex$ extra observations in addition to the typical bandit feedback, there exists a loss sequence $\ell_{1:T}$ (which may depend on both $\pi$ and $\Bex$) such that 
    \begin{equation*}
        \!\ex{R_T^{\pi}(\ell_{1:T})}\!=\!\left\{
        \begin{aligned}
        &\wtOmega(\PTP), \!\!\!\!&\!\Bex=O(\PTP), \\
        &\wtOmega(T\sqrt{K/\Bex}), \!\!\!\!&\!\Bex=\Omega(\PTP).
        \end{aligned}
        \right.
    \end{equation*}

In the setting of bandit learning with switching costs under an extra observation budget $\Bex \in [0, (K-1)T]$, the minimax regret is given by
    \begin{equation*}
        R_T^*=\left\{
        \begin{aligned}
        &\wtTheta(\PTP), & \Bex=O(\PTP), \\
        &\wtTheta(T\sqrt{K/\Bex}), & \Bex=\Omega(\PTP).
        \end{aligned}
        \right.
    \end{equation*}
